  "description": "Ywith a Fuji Touring, but\nif you're anything like the guys at Fuji, you're gonna want to travel\nunfamiliar blue-line highways on this bicycle. Maybe ride it to your reunion.\nFuji's product guys designed this bike for comfortable loaded touring.\nThe angles of the butted, cro-moly frame are relaxed for stability, the\nwheelbase is long, the clearances around the wheels sufficient for fat,\nsturdy tires and fenders.\n\nThe wheels are especially strong, each built with 36, 14-gauge spokes\nlaced into strong, double-wall aluminum rims with Vittoria long-distance\ntires on them.\n\nThe drivetrain, upgraded this year, is a mix of Shimano's road and mountain\ncomponents. It's a wide-range 27-speed Shimano Tiagra/Deore setup, gears\nfor the Smokies (up and down) and the desert southwest. The powerful,\nsimple, cantilever brakes are upgraded this year, too.\n\nEach Touring comes with a rack, improved for 2002 by the way, and a spare-spoke-holder\non one chainstay. Thr fork is also drilled for the ultra-stable low rider\nracks if your really going to carry a load.\n\nYou can buy a Touring and never leave town. But if, come spring, you find\nyourself unfolding maps and staring out your office",
